      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Watershed playground: separating touching blobs\n\nPlain thresholding fuses touching objects into one contour. The watershed recipe: Otsu binary -> open (drop specks) -> the blob cores via distanceTransform (pixels far from any background survive a high threshold on the normalized distance - one core per object even when they touch) -> dilate the binary for the sure-background rim; between them lies the 'unknown' band where cv2.watershed floods from the cores and draws -1 boundary lines where two floods meet. The 'Watershed markers' subgraph builds the int32 seed map from generic arithmetic: connected-component labels + 1, unknown band zeroed. A blank image flows through with seeds=1 and no boundaries - nothing raises."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
